---
/*
 * The media wrapper. `Image.svelte` and `Video.svelte` are the SvelteKit files copied
 * verbatim; this file is the whole cost of keeping them Svelte, because a markdoc
 * `render:` cannot point at a `.svelte` file directly.
 *
 * It dispatches BOTH media components rather than there being an Img.astro and a
 * Vid.astro, because of finding 07-1: `content-entry-type.js` builds the TAG component
 * map from `getUsedTags(ast)` — only tags the document literally writes — while the NODE
 * map is built unfiltered. Nothing writes `{% vid %}` (the paragraph transform
 * synthesises it), so a marker on `tags.vid` is never resolved and Svelte receives the
 * raw marker object: `TypeError: component is not a function`, after ~4 pages have built.
 * So: one marker, on `nodes.image`, and the fork lives here. One fewer file than priced.
 */
import Image from '../lib/media/Image.svelte'
import Video from '../lib/media/Video.svelte'

// `class` is a reserved word in the destructuring position, hence the rename.
//
// `description` is split out because the two branches want different things, exactly as
// SvelteKit's two branches did: its `img` Tag carried `{...attributes, description,
// aspectRatio}` while its `vid` Tag carried the attributes alone. The Astro transform
// cannot make that distinction — the fork moved here (07-1) — so it forwards
// `description` unconditionally and this is where the video branch drops it again.
//
// It is not cosmetic. `Video.svelte` does not declare a `description` prop, so the value
// falls into its `...rest` and spreads onto the element: every one of the 16 video
// figures renders `<figure ... description="">` where the SvelteKit prerender has no
// such attribute. Inert, invisible, and a parity difference on all 16.
//
// FINDING (16-1). `<Image />` server-renders with NO `client:` directive; only `<Video />`
// keeps one. 14-2 established the island was inert here — `visible` is initialised `true`
// and `blurDataUrl` has had no producer since ticket 10 — and deliberately left this file
// alone, recording the inconsistency rather than fixing it. 16 is where the deferred half
// came due: `<astro-island>` is `display: contents`, so it generates no box, but CSS
// SELECTORS match the DOM tree, not the box tree. Every `>`-combinator rule aimed at a
// figure landed on the island instead, and the figure fell through to auto-placement.
const { class: className, image_isvideo, description, ...rest } = Astro.props
---

{
  image_isvideo ? (
    <Video client:visible class={className} {...rest} />
  ) : (
    <Image class={className} description={description} {...rest} />
  )
}
